# Citation metadata for the fitpo software (https://citation-file-format.github.io).
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use fitpo, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
type: software
title: fitpo
abstract: >-
  fitpo fits piecewise-linear (bilinear, trilinear and quadrilinear)
  backbones to nonlinear pushover curves by minimising the area between the
  backbone and the curve, to define equivalent single-degree-of-freedom
  systems of complex structures. It includes the fits of De Luca et al.
  (2013), fits for concentrically braced frames with brace fracture, and
  envelope extraction from cyclic pushover data.
authors:
  - family-names: Clemett
    given-names: Nicholas
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3733-4971"
    affiliation: Helmut-Schmidt-Universität
# Uncomment and fill in at each release, e.g. version "0.1.0" and the date
# in YYYY-MM-DD form; until then they are left out so the file validates.
# version: "0.1.0"
# date-released: "YYYY-MM-DD"
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
repository-code: "https://github.com/nc-hsu/fitpo"
url: "https://fitpo.readthedocs.io"
keywords:
  - pushover analysis
  - capacity curve
  - backbone curve
  - piecewise linear fit
  - equivalent SDOF
  - earthquake engineering
  - concentrically braced frames
references:
  - type: article
    title: >-
      Near-optimal piecewise linear fits of static pushover capacity curves
      for equivalent SDOF analysis
    authors:
      - family-names: De Luca
        given-names: F.
      - family-names: Vamvatsikos
        given-names: D.
      - family-names: Iervolino
        given-names: I.
    journal: Earthquake Engineering & Structural Dynamics
    volume: 42
    issue: 4
    start: 523
    end: 543
    year: 2013
    doi: 10.1002/eqe.2225
